Beryllium: keep toolbar buttons full height in Helium's vertical layouts

Purpose: with "Show home button" on, the owner saw the address bar move
  over but no Home button, no tooltip and no response in its place
  (16.0-CURRENT, 3 November 2026; the same with --disable-gpu-compositing,
  so not a drawing fault). freebsd/tests/browser/run ui read the window
  through UI DevTools in each Helium layout: classic, centered address
  bar, minimal URL, compact and zen mode with the top bar pinned are
  fine; in "vertical tabs" (left or right) and "dynamic", and in the
  owner's own settings, the Home button is laid out 28 x 0 px. So are
  the Forward button and Helium's "Collapse tabs" button. Back and Reload
  are 28 x 31.
  Cause: helium/ui/layout/toolbar-overflow.patch gives every toolbar
  button that can move to the overflow menu the flex rule
  FlexSpecification(kPreferredSnapToZero, kPreferred). That constructor
  takes no orientation and applies the rule to both axes, so a button
  snaps to zero height whenever the toolbar's height leaves less than its
  preferred height. The toolbar has a 3 px interior margin above and
  below; in the classic layout it is 37 px tall (31 px left, buttons fit),
  in the vertical tabs and dynamic layouts 34 px (28 px left), and every
  such button collapses. Back and Reload have kPreferred rules from
  helium/ui/layout/toolbar-layout.patch and keep their height.
  Chromium's own ToolbarController uses the horizontal-only form of this
  rule, which this patch now uses too: buttons still drop into the
  overflow menu when the toolbar is too narrow, and keep their height
  (31 px, as Back and Reload) when it is too short.
  Not FreeBSD-specific: the layout code is the same on every platform.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on helium/ui/layout/toolbar-overflow.patch
  (stage 3), which adds the loop this changes.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench.
Test: freebsd/tests/browser/run ui (every layout row "fine"; the test also
  fails on any visible toolbar button with no height).
security-review: not required (layout only)

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc
@@ -1947,7 +1947,13 @@
             overflow_order, child->GetProperty(views::kElementIdentifierKey))) {
       continue;
     }
+    // Beryllium: snap to zero along the toolbar only. Without an orientation
+    // the rule also applies to height, and in the vertical tabs and dynamic
+    // layouts the toolbar leaves 28 px for 31 px buttons, so Home, Forward
+    // and Collapse tabs were laid out zero pixels tall: invisible, with no
+    // tooltip, while the address bar still moved over for them.
     auto responsive = views::FlexSpecification(
+        views::LayoutOrientation::kHorizontal,
         views::MinimumFlexSizeRule::kPreferredSnapToZero,
         views::MaximumFlexSizeRule::kPreferred);
     if (const auto* flex = child->GetProperty(views::kFlexBehaviorKey)) {
